# Skill Surface — cursor-sdk seat

**Seat wall.** The IDE rule is pruned from this dispatch HOME. You have no skill
picker to refresh, no Reload Window, and no claude.ai Customize session — those are
lead duties. One obligation survives, and it is a real one.

## Invariant

```
edit(cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/{skills,commands,rules}/ ∨ census)
  ⇒ run(scripts/cursor/install-ecosystem-plugin.sh) in this dispatch
```

Installed plugin trees are **copies** (`cp -a`), not links. Editing the SoT under
`cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/` changes nothing live until the install script copies
it into `~/.cursor/plugins/local/ulg-ecosystem/`. An SoT edit without the install is
**landed, not live** — report it that way, or run the script and say you did.

| SoT path you touched | Install required? |
|---|---|
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/skills/` (census) | **Yes** |
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/commands/` | **Yes** |
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem/rules/*_ulg.mdc` (+ `RULES_ULG_CENSUS`) | **Yes** |
| `{repo}/.cursor/skills/` or `*_ws.mdc` | No — checkout-local, read live |
| `cursor-plugins/ulg-ecosystem-seats/` | No — read from SoT at dispatch setup |

## Not yours

Claude-slug bundle regeneration and Customize upload, `SKILLS_CENSUS` membership
decisions, and picker-staleness notes: **do not attempt**. If your work implies one,
name it in the closeout and let the lead route it.

## Skill bodies

Say `Use the `{slug}` skill` and let the harness fetch it. Do **not** `fs`-read a
`SKILL.md` into context to "load" a skill — that is the authoring path, not the
consumption path, and it burns the budget the skill layer exists to save.

